CommitDate: Tue Nov 3 18:38:26 2026 +1100

    fix: share consuming class commands between factory trials and execution
    
    Own quoted names and complete multiline bodies, preserve native declarations
    and modifier state, execute mixing in order, and retain container aliases and
    canonical note targets. Render native leaf spots and declaration visibility
    from Java's header and VisibilityModifier model. Keep actor-only generalization
    on its valid description path after a rejected class trial.
    
    Precommitted causal accounts:
    - 2a0981759c523c9da3d19ebc7f7919bb4cdd3fec (commands, container aliases)
    - be918a98f6e445c13e29d6f314f0f1dfa13b9acb (native leaf presentation)
    - 902086e529d4eb564bce381458995048b580c5be (note target quarks)
    - bc0c65b6aad9cf98995fba162ccb9ee3b16613c4 (quoted code identity)
    - 93dd8e2f5edd728607704f3d72a7c09a09fe7d9a (description trial fallback)
    
    Unimplemented blocking renderer dependencies are recorded in
     eb5b550fe22d246a5dee048bf7396cd70de0378d.
    
    Maker results: workspace lib 1420/1420; parser 566/566; parser Clippy clean.
    Prepared perturbations 383/833 (was 349/833), including 12/23 prior checker
    inputs; 22/31 fresh valid CLI cases. Main tiers unchanged at 11181/11251 and
    10497/11251, with identical failure inventories. Both main tier gates and
    perturbation gate remain red; guards 4/6. No acceptance claim. Mixed leaf
    paint, page chrome, cloud coordinates and note layout still block parity.

